SUMMARY:Horizon flux-balance laws in the multiscale perturbation
DESCRIPTION:Séminaire Amplitudes et Gravitation sur l'Yvette (IHES/IPhT) I
  study the evolution of the event horizon in a “two-timescale” perturb
 ative expansion around a stationary black hole. This leads to strong const
 raints on the “coarse-grained” horizon dynamics. At leading order\, th
 e horizon exhibits an “adiabatic rigidity”: the leading corrections to
  its angular velocity and inaffinity remain uniform…\nhttps://indico.mat
